    {
     "user": "go test -race fails intermittently in CI for the index package"
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "go test -race ./internal/index",
      "output": "==================\nWARNING: DATA RACE\nWrite at 0x00c0001a2150 by goroutine 14:\n  quarry/internal/index.(*Index).Add()\n      /src/internal/index/index.go:41 +0x8c\n\nPrevious read at 0x00c0001a2150 by goroutine 13:\n  quarry/internal/index.(*Index).Lookup()\n      /src/internal/index/index.go:58 +0x64\n==================\n--- FAIL: TestConcurrentAddLookup (0.02s)\nFAIL\nFAIL\tquarry/internal/index\t0.318s",
      "exit": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "assistant": "Add writes the postings map while Lookup reads it with no synchronization. sync.Map would allocate on every Lookup; a sync.RWMutex around the map is enough."
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "go test -race -count=20 ./internal/index",
      "output": "ok  \tquarry/internal/index\t4.212s",
      "exit": 0
     }
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qr-002",
   "project": "quarry",
   "harness": "claude",
   "age_days": 60,
   "turns": [
    {
     "user": "p99 latency spikes every few seconds on the quarry box, suspect GC"
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "GODEBUG=gctrace=1 ./quarry --replay trace.log 2>&1 | tail -2",
      "output": "gc 187 @39.8s 13%: 0.05+30+0.02 ms clock, 598->631->298 MB, 640 MB goal, 8 P\ngc 188 @40.3s 14%: 0.05+31+0.02 ms clock, 612->640->301 MB, 640 MB goal, 8 P",
      "exit": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "./loadtest --gogc 100 && ./loadtest --gogc 400",
      "output": "GOGC=100 p99=80ms rss=640MB\nGOGC=400 p99=31ms rss=1.7GB",
      "exit": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "journalctl -u quarry -n 2 --no-pager",
      "output": "kernel: Out of memory: Killed process 2211 (quarry) total-vm:2210468kB\nsystemd[1]: quarry.service: Main process exited, code=killed, status=9/KILL",
      "exit": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "user": "No. The cgroup is 1GiB so GOGC=400 gets us OOM killed. And do not use sync.Pool for postings, the benchmark showed no win. Set GOMEMLIMIT and keep GOGC moderate."
    },
    {
     "tool": {
      "cmd": "GOMEMLIMIT=900MiB GOGC=200 ./loadtest",
      "output": "p99=34ms rss=870MB",
      "exit": 0
     }
    }
   ]
  },
